---
/**
 * About Us `#doctors` — the charcoal band that introduces the two doctors: a
 * centred SectionIntro over two alternating `article.doc-grid`s, each an
 * <ImageFrame> (main portrait + inset) beside a `.doc-copy` column of eyebrow,
 * h2, `.role` line, lead, two bios, three credential tiles and two buttons.
 *
 * A code_section band, registered as `about_us_doctors` in
 * src/blocks/CodeSectionBlock.astro (plan decision D6, 2026-09-08: this band
 * stays code, byte-identical; a media_split extension that could hold the
 * inset, the role line and the intro trio is a later round). The section's id
 * arrives as `id`, the prop name CodeSectionBlock defaults to, and defaults to
 * the "doctors" the template has always rendered — the hero's second CTA links
 * `#doctors` (about-us/index.astro:389), so the default must hold when a row is
 * saved with a blank anchor.
 *
 * ── D1: a route-scoped band reads its own page ────────────────────────────
 * Everything the template reads from WordPress on this band is read here the
 * same way, through `getPageContent(Astro.url.pathname)` — the read the page
 * runs at about-us/index.astro:49 — guarded by the `route` prop: on any other
 * route the band renders NOTHING and warns, because the rows and slots it
 * asks for exist only on the About Us entry (plan decision D1, 2026-09-08;
 * TrustStrip.astro is the first precedent, this is the same idiom).
 *
 * ── What is live and what is literal ──────────────────────────────────────
 * Live (Pages -> About Us in wp-admin):
 *   - Section copy row `doctors-intro` through introFrom() with the template's
 *     literals as the fallback (about-us/index.astro:353; introFrom is
 *     src/lib/page-content.ts:503-521) → the SectionIntro's eyebrow, heading,
 *     headingItalic and lede.
 *   - Section copy row `doctors`: `heading` (set:html, "Dr. Bryce
 *     <em>Richardson</em>" live) and `body` (Dr. Richardson's `p.lead`) —
 *     about-us/index.astro:495 and :497. The row's eyebrow is NOT read; the
 *     template never read it either (the eyebrow is the literal at :494).
 *   - Images slots drBryceMain, drBryceInset, drAnnieMain, drAnnieInset
 *     (url/width/height; about-us/index.astro:480-491 and :579-590).
 * Literal, exactly as the template has them: both eyebrows (:494, :535), both
 * `.role` lines (:496, :537), the four image alts (:484, :490, :583, :589 —
 * every one of these slots carries alt null live, so the template's words
 * are the only alts there are), Dr. Richardson's two bios (:498-512), ALL of
 * Dr. Annie's copy (:536-555 — no Section-copy row exists for her; recorded
 * in plan-decisions.json owner_side_not_gating), the six credential tiles
 * (:513-523, :557-570) and the four buttons (:525-526, :573-576).
 *
 * ── Markup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Verbatim from about-us/index.astro:466-594 — element order, class strings,
 * attributes, entities — plus 58 `{" "}` whitespace shims that exist for one
 * measured reason:
 *
 * THE ROOT-EXPRESSION WHITESPACE RULE (measured through @astrojs/compiler
 * 3.0.1 with `compact: true`, the flag Astro passes from compressHTML,
 * 2026-09-08). At a template's top level, compressHTML collapses every
 * whitespace-only run between two tags to ONE space — that is why
 * dist/about-us/index.html reads `<section …> <div class="wrap" …> <div class=
 * "vs-intro-triad …`. Inside an expression that holds the template's FIRST
 * element (`{band && (<section>…)}` here; the same shape as PaymentBand's
 * `{hasBand && (…)}`, whose band ships `<section …><div class="wrap"…>` with
 * no spaces on /general-dentistry/), the compiler STRIPS those runs instead.
 * No byte-free predecessor flips it back (a leading <style>, <slot />, HTML
 * comment, <Fragment />, or `{false && <i />}` were each tried; only a real
 * root element does, and a real element is bytes). So every run the template
 * ships as a space is written here as an explicit `{" "}` — a string-literal
 * expression renders exactly one space, and it does not touch the text-node
 * rules below — and the two runs the template ships as TWO spaces (either
 * side of the JSX comment expressions "Dr. Richardson — image LEFT" at :477
 * and "Dr. Annie — image RIGHT" at :532; a comment expression renders
 * nothing but keeps the whitespace on both sides of itself) are written
 * `{" "}` + the same comment + `{" "}`. (The comment delimiters are not
 * spelled out in this header: a star-slash inside a JSDoc block ends the
 * block early and the compiled module stops parsing — caught by
 * `node --check` on the compiled output, which the compiler's own
 * diagnostics do not cover.) Proof: the band compiled through the same compiler is
 * byte-identical to lines 466-594 of the template compiled the same way, with
 * every `${…}` normalised (3381 = 3381 bytes; the two D1 reads are the only
 * expressions that differ in source).
 *
 * The multi-line text nodes (lead, bios, one `.v` tile) keep their
 * continuation lines at the template's 16 spaces: compressHTML collapses only
 * the leading and trailing whitespace run of a text node to "\n" and ships
 * every interior "\n" + indentation run as-is, so the indentation of those
 * lines IS output. They are literal text, not expressions, for a second
 * reason: an expression HTML-escapes the apostrophes ("patient's" would ship
 * as "patient&#39;s") and the second bio carries `<em>Full Arch Masters</em>`
 * inline.
 *
 * ── CSS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Every about-us.css rule that reaches an element on this band is restated
 * below with the value that WINS on the charcoal band today, rooted at least
 * two compounds deep. Astro compiles ATTRIBUTE scoping, so a bare `.doc-grid`
 * would be `.doc-grid[data-astro-cid-…]` = (0,2,0), a dead tie with the
 * sheet's `.aus .doc-grid` decided by bundle order (CodeSectionBlock.astro:
 * 437-439 records the precedent; PaymentBand.astro carries the same note).
 * Rooting at `.section` puts every rule at (0,4,0)+ and the band owns its box
 * whether or not the page sheet is in the cascade. Elements drawn by child
 * components (SectionIntro's triad, h2 and lede; ImageFrame's `.vs-frame`;
 * the `<em>` inside a set:html heading) carry no scope attribute, so those
 * compounds are written `:global(…)` — the scoped root still carries the
 * attribute and the specificity.
 *
 * NOT restated, on purpose: global.css rules (.vs-h2, .vs-lede, .vs-eyebrow,
 * .vs-frame, .vs-btn-*, .vs-intro-triad) — they are global on every route and
 * the page sheet does not override them except where restated here; and
 * about-us.css:114-116 (`.section.alt .eyebrow`), which matches NO element on
 * this band — every eyebrow here is the <Eyebrow> component's `.vs-eyebrow`
 * (the page map records the same grep: 0 matches for class `eyebrow`).
 */
import Button from "./Button.astro";
import Eyebrow from "./Eyebrow.astro";
import SectionIntro from "./SectionIntro.astro";
import ImageFrame from "./ImageFrame.astro";
import { getPageContent, introFrom, type PageImage } from "../lib/page-content";
import { bookNowHref } from "../data/contact";

interface Props {
  /**
   * The route this band belongs to ("/about-us/"). It reads that page's
   * Section copy and image slots, so on any other route it renders nothing
   * and warns.
   */
  route: string;
  /**
   * The DOM id. Defaults to "doctors" (about-us/index.astro:466), which the
   * hero's second CTA links. CodeSectionBlock overrides it with the row's
   * deduplicated anchor — that override is the point of its `anchorProp`.
   */
  id?: string;
}

const { route, id = "doctors" } = Astro.props;

// trailingSlash is 'always' (astro.config.mjs:21); normalise both sides anyway
// so "/about-us" and "/about-us/" name the same page, as page-content.ts does.
const withSlash = (p: string) => (p.endsWith("/") ? p : `${p}/`);
const here = Astro.url.pathname;
const onRoute = withSlash(here) === withSlash(route);

if (!onRoute) {
  console.warn(
    `[blocks] DoctorsBand is scoped to ${route} and was asked to render on ${here} — it reads that page's Section copy and image slots, so it renders nothing here`,
  );
}

type Band = {
  intro: { eyebrow: string; heading: string; headingItalic: string; lede: string };
  /** sections[doctors].heading — html-bearing, rendered with set:html. */
  heading: string;
  /** sections[doctors].body — Dr. Richardson's `p.lead`. */
  lead: string;
  drBryceMain: PageImage;
  drBryceInset: PageImage;
  drAnnieMain: PageImage;
  drAnnieInset: PageImage;
};

let band: Band | null = null;
if (onRoute) {
  const { section, image } = await getPageContent(here);
  band = {
    // about-us/index.astro:353 — the same defaults, so the page is
    // byte-identical until the row is edited in wp-admin.
    intro: introFrom(section("doctors-intro"), { eyebrow: "Meet the Doctors", heading: "Two practitioners.", headingItalic: "One philosophy.", lede: "Dr. Bryce Richardson and Dr. Annelise Westermeier lead a small, focused team. Together they bring cosmetic mastery and holistic surgical care under one roof, so every patient finds the right hands for the right work." }),
    heading: section("doctors").heading,
    lead: section("doctors").body,
    drBryceMain: image("drBryceMain"),
    drBryceInset: image("drBryceInset"),
    drAnnieMain: image("drAnnieMain"),
    drAnnieInset: image("drAnnieInset"),
  };
}
---

{
  band && (
      <section class="section alt" id={id}>{" "}
        <div class="wrap" data-vs-reveal-batch>{" "}
          <SectionIntro
            eyebrow={band.intro.eyebrow}
            heading={band.intro.heading}
            headingItalic={band.intro.headingItalic}
            lede={band.intro.lede}
            centered
            class="aus-section-head"
          />{" "}

          {/* Dr. Richardson — image LEFT */}{" "}
          <article class="doc-grid" id="dr-richardson">{" "}
            <ImageFrame
              primary={{
                src: band.drBryceMain.url,
                width: band.drBryceMain.width,
                height: band.drBryceMain.height,
                alt: 'Dr. Bryce Richardson, founder of Vivid Smiles Dentistry',
              }}
              inset={{
                src: band.drBryceInset.url,
                width: band.drBryceInset.width,
                height: band.drBryceInset.height,
                alt: 'Dr. Richardson performing precise dental work in surgical loupes',
              }}
            />{" "}
            <div class="doc-copy" data-vs-reveal-batch>{" "}
              <Eyebrow>Founder &amp; Cosmetic Lead</Eyebrow>{" "}
              <h2 class="vs-h2"><Fragment set:html={band.heading} /></h2>{" "}
              <div class="role">Cosmetic, full-arch &amp; implant dentistry</div>{" "}
              <p class="lead">{band.lead}</p>{" "}
              <p class="bio">
                A graduate of Indiana University School of Dentistry, Dr. Richardson has completed
                more than 600 hours of advanced postgraduate training in esthetics, veneers,
                full-mouth rehabilitation, and surgical dentistry. His cosmetic philosophy centers
                on designing smiles that harmonize with each patient's facial features, personality,
                and lifestyle, so the final result feels effortless, youthful, and authentically
                you.
              </p>{" "}
              <p class="bio">
                He also serves as a mentor for <em>Full Arch Masters</em>, one of the nation's
                premier implant education programs, training doctors across the country in advanced
                surgical and full-arch procedures. Outside the office, Dr. Richardson enjoys
                traveling, playing golf, and spending time with his wife and their three dogs.
              </p>{" "}

              <div class="doc-credentials">{" "}
                <div class="cred">{" "}
                  <div class="k">IU</div><div class="v">School of Dentistry Graduate</div>{" "}
                </div>{" "}
                <div class="cred">{" "}
                  <div class="k">600+</div><div class="v">Hours Postgrad Training</div>{" "}
                </div>{" "}
                <div class="cred">{" "}
                  <div class="k">FAM</div><div class="v">Full Arch Masters Mentor</div>{" "}
                </div>{" "}
              </div>{" "}

              <div class="doc-actions">{" "}
                <Button variant="light" href={bookNowHref}>Book Online</Button>{" "}
                <Button variant="ghost-light" href="/smile-gallery/">See Case Portfolio</Button>{" "}
              </div>{" "}
            </div>{" "}
          </article>{" "}

          {/* Dr. Annie — image RIGHT */}{" "}
          <article class="doc-grid image-right" id="dr-annie">{" "}
            <div class="doc-copy" data-vs-reveal-batch>{" "}
              <Eyebrow>General &amp; Holistic Care</Eyebrow>{" "}
              <h2 class="vs-h2">Dr. Annelise<br /><em>Westermeier</em></h2>{" "}
              <div class="role">Known to patients as <em>Dr. Annie</em></div>{" "}
              <p class="lead">
                A fourth-generation dentist practicing with the warmth of family tradition and the
                rigor of modern clinical training.
              </p>{" "}
              <p class="bio">
                Dr. Annie attended the University at Buffalo School of Dental Medicine in her
                hometown of Buffalo, NY, alongside her brother, before completing her Advanced
                Education in General Dentistry at Virginia Commonwealth University. That residency
                deepened her expertise in surgery, implants, and the care of medically complex
                patients.
              </p>{" "}
              <p class="bio">
                Her approach is holistic: she treats the mouth as inseparable from the rest of the
                body, and the patient as a person first. She is passionate about making every visit
                feel comfortable, unhurried, and collaborative, and will undoubtedly coax a smile
                from even the most nervous of patients. Whether you are in pain or simply want to
                eat and smile more freely, Dr. Annie is eager to care for you.
              </p>{" "}

              <div class="doc-credentials">{" "}
                <div class="cred">{" "}
                  <div class="k">UB</div><div class="v">Buffalo School of Dental Medicine</div>{" "}
                </div>{" "}
                <div class="cred">{" "}
                  <div class="k">VCU</div><div class="v">
                    Advanced Education in General Dentistry
                  </div>{" "}
                </div>{" "}
                <div class="cred">{" "}
                  <div class="k">4th</div><div class="v">Generation Dentist</div>{" "}
                </div>{" "}
              </div>{" "}

              <div class="doc-actions">{" "}
                <Button variant="light" href={bookNowHref}>Book with Dr. Annie</Button>{" "}
                <Button variant="ghost-light" href="/general-dentistry/"
                  >Learn About Holistic Care</Button
                >{" "}
              </div>{" "}
            </div>{" "}
            <ImageFrame
              primary={{
                src: band.drAnnieMain.url,
                width: band.drAnnieMain.width,
                height: band.drAnnieMain.height,
                alt: 'Dr. Annelise Westermeier, general & holistic dentist at Vivid Smiles',
              }}
              inset={{
                src: band.drAnnieInset.url,
                width: band.drAnnieInset.width,
                height: band.drAnnieInset.height,
                alt: 'Dr. Annelise Westermeier in the Vivid Smiles Dentistry office',
              }}
            />{" "}
          </article>{" "}
        </div>{" "}
      </section>
  )
}

<style>
  /*
   * Copied out of src/styles/pages/about-us.css — every rule cited by line,
   * carrying the value that wins on the charcoal `.section.alt` band today.
   * The page sheet is NOT edited; these duplicates outrank it (see the CSS
   * note in the header), so the band draws the same box from either sheet.
   */

  /* ---- band chrome ---- */

  /* css:103 (`.aus .section`). `section.section` rather than `.section` so the
     scoped rule is (0,2,1) against the sheet's (0,2,0) — a win, not a tie.
     global.css:642-644 pads every <section> by --vs-section-pad; the sheet's
     110px has always beaten that here and does again. */
  section.section {
    padding: 110px 0;
  }
  /* css:107 */
  section.section.alt {
    background: var(--vs-charcoal-green);
  }
  /* css:32 */
  .section .wrap {
    max-width: 1240px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 40px;
  }
  /* css:136 — the SectionIntro's box. Its root is a child component's
     element, hence :global. SectionIntro.astro's own global
     `.vs-intro-triad-center { margin-inline: auto }` is (0,1,0) and has
     always lost the margin to this (0,2,0) rule; same value either way. */
  .section :global(.aus-section-head) {
    margin: 0 auto 64px;
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  /* ---- typography the band inherits from the page's h2 / p / em rules ----
     Both h2s on this band carry `.vs-h2` (global.css:489-497); the page sheet
     out-specifies it on font-size and letter-spacing (css:34-40) and the
     charcoal band on colour (css:108-113). The SectionIntro's h2, lede and em
     are child-component elements, so the element compounds are :global. */

  /* css:34-40 with css:108-110's `#fff` — the value that wins inside .alt.
     `.aus h2 { color: var(--vs-ink) }` at css:495 is (0,1,1) and loses to
     (0,3,1) here as it does in the sheet. */
  .section.alt .wrap :global(h2) {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.2vw, 54px);
    color: #fff;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
  }
  /* css:41 + css:44 (italic, weight 300) with css:111-112's colour. Covers
     the intro h2's `em.vs-italic-word` (global.css:535-538 says
     `font-weight: inherit`, and `.aus h2 em` at (0,1,2) has always beaten it
     to 300), the set:html `<em>Richardson</em>`, `<em>Westermeier</em>`, the
     two `.role` ems and the bio's `<em>Full Arch Masters</em>`. */
  .section.alt .wrap :global(em) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--vs-eyebrow-on-sage);
    font-weight: 300;
  }
  /* css:43 with css:113's colour. The lede (`.vs-lede`, global.css:518-524,
     ink-soft at (0,1,0)) has always taken this colour from (0,3,1). */
  .section.alt .wrap :global(p) {
    margin: 0;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
  }

  /* ---- the two doctor rows ---- */

  /* css:185-189 */
  .section .doc-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.05fr;
    gap: 80px;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 110px;
  }
  /* css:190 */
  .section .doc-grid:last-of-type {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  /* css:191 */
  .section .doc-grid.image-right {
    grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 1fr;
  }

  /* css:193 — must beat the `margin: 0` restated above, as it does in the
     sheet. Rooted with `.alt` so it is (0,6,1) against that rule's (0,5,1):
     a win, not a same-file tie left to source order. */
  .section.alt .doc-copy h2 {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  /* css:194-199 with css:211's charcoal colour. */
  .section.alt .doc-copy .role {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--vs-eyebrow-on-sage);
    font-size: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  /* css:200-202 with css:212's `#fff`. */
  .section.alt .doc-copy .lead {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: #fff;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  /* css:203-206 with css:213's colour. */
  .section.alt .doc-copy .bio {
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
  }

  /* css:214-218 with css:231's rule colour. */
  .section.alt .doc-credentials {
    margin-top: 42px;
    padding-top: 34px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 28px;
  }
  /* css:219-223 with css:232's colour. */
  .section.alt .doc-credentials .cred .k {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display);
    font-size: 36px;
    color: var(--vs-eyebrow-on-sage);
    line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  /* css:224-228 with css:233's colour. */
  .section.alt .doc-credentials .cred .v {
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);
    margin-top: 10px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  /* css:234-237 */
  .section .doc-actions {
    margin-top: 40px;
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  /* ---- responsive ---- */

  /* css:433-446 */
  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .section .doc-grid,
    .section .doc-grid.image-right {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 50px;
    }
    /* When the doctor grid stacks, the image must always sit ABOVE the copy —
       even in the .image-right variant where DOM order has copy first.
       `.vs-frame` is ImageFrame's root, hence :global. */
    .section .doc-grid.image-right > .doc-copy {
      order: 2;
    }
    .section .doc-grid.image-right > :global(.vs-frame) {
      order: 1;
    }
  }

  /* css:465-472 */
  @media (max-width: 780px) {
    .section .wrap {
      padding: 0 22px;
    }
    section.section {
      padding: 70px 0;
    }
    .section .doc-grid {
      margin-bottom: 70px;
    }
    .section.alt .doc-credentials {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 22px;
    }
    .section.alt .doc-credentials .cred .k {
      font-size: 30px;
    }
  }
</style>
